{
  "id": "27840_tsumu",
  "headword": "{詰|つ}む",
  "reading": "つむ",
  "romaji": "tsumu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to be checkmated; to be cornered; to be stuck",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to be checkmated; to be cornered; to have no way out",
      "explanation": "Originally a shogi/chess term for the king being checkmated. By extension, used colloquially to mean a situation is hopeless and there is no escape."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27840_tsumu_ex1",
      "japanese": "これでもう{詰|つ}んだ。",
      "english": "That's it, it's all over now.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27840_tsumu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{王|おう}が{詰|つ}んで{勝負|しょうぶ}がついた。",
      "english": "The king was checkmated and the game was decided.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27840_tsumu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{締|し}め{切|き}りが{明日|あした}なのに{何|なに}も{終|お}わっていなくて、もう{詰|つ}んでいる。",
      "english": "The deadline is tomorrow and nothing is done — I'm completely stuck.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A shogi/chess term for checkmate, now widely used as casual slang for a hopeless situation with no remaining options. The slang sense is very common online and in conversation among younger speakers.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {王|おう}が{詰|つ}む: the king is checkmated\n- もう{詰|つ}んだ: it's hopeless now\n- {人生|じんせい}{詰|つ}んだ: my life is over (hyperbolic slang)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {摘|つ}む: to pluck; to pick — unrelated homophone\n- {積|つ}む: to pile up; to load — unrelated homophone",
